# ===== Dialogue Editor top menu (Adobe style) =====
# ===== Menu titles =====
menu_line => Line
menu_char => Character
menu_text => Text
menu_file => File
menu_help => Help

# ===== Status bar =====
status_line => Line:
status_char => Char:
status_anim => Anim:
status_speed => Speed:

# ===== Items: Line menu =====
item_prev_line => Previous line
item_next_line => Next line
item_add_line => Insert new line after current
item_remove_line => Delete current line

# ===== Items: Character menu =====
item_char => Character file
label_char => Character file
item_angry => Angry bubble
label_angry => Angry bubble
item_speed => Type speed (sec/char)
label_speed => Type speed
item_sound => Type sound
label_sound => Type sound
item_replay_text => Replay current line text
item_prev_anim => Previous expression
item_next_anim => Next expression

# ===== Items: Text menu =====
item_text => Dialogue text
label_text => Dialogue text

# ===== Items: File menu =====
item_load => Load dialogue (JSON)
item_save => Save dialogue (JSON)
item_exit => Exit editor

# ===== Descriptions (hover row footer) =====
desc_prev_line => Switch to the previous dialogue line
desc_next_line => Switch to the next dialogue line
desc_add_line => Insert a new dialogue line after the selected one and select it
desc_remove_line => Delete the currently selected dialogue line
desc_char => Character JSON file used for the portrait (under images/dialogue/)
desc_angry => Use the red "angry" speech bubble style for this line
desc_speed => Type speed: smaller values type faster (sec/char)
desc_sound => Type sound file name (under sounds/, empty uses default)
desc_text => The dialogue text shown for this line (Shift+Enter adds a line break)
desc_replay_text => Replay the typing animation of the current line text
desc_prev_anim => Switch to the previous expression animation
desc_next_anim => Switch to the next expression animation
desc_load => Load a dialogue JSON file from disk
desc_save => Save the current dialogue as a dialogue JSON file
desc_exit => Exit the dialogue editor and return to the master editor menu (confirms when unsaved changes exist)

# ===== Help (read-only text rows) =====
item_help_nav => Previous/next line: A / D
item_help_anims => Previous/next expression: W / S
item_help_replay => Replay text: SPACE
item_help_f1 => Open this help menu: F1
item_help_exit => Exit editor: ESC

# ===== Help row descriptions =====
desc_help_nav => Previous/next line: A / D
desc_help_anims => Previous/next expression: W / S
desc_help_replay => Replay current line text: SPACE
desc_help_f1 => Open this help menu: F1
desc_help_exit => Exit editor: ESC (confirms when unsaved changes exist)

# ===== Exit confirmation popup (overrides the shared keys in the editors group) =====
confirm_unsaved_title => Exit Dialogue Editor
confirm_unsaved_message => This dialogue has unsaved changes. Those lines will be lost if you exit. Discard them and exit?
